{#
«فيديو عائم» — the floating corner video (like YouTube / Facebook) of the
«بانر أو فيديو» block (home/qissa-media), the one video block that has the switch.

The block has a «mini_player» switch. Off: it is a banner with its own place in
the page, as always. On: the block renders nothing in the page and includes this
partial instead — the video has no place in the page and sits in the bottom-left
corner of the screen (WhatsApp sits bottom-right), over the store, from the
moment the page has loaded. Two buttons: enlarge (centred over the page) and
close (gone for this page view).

Review of 24 Nov 2026 (the brand could neither move it nor control it enlarged):
  - DRAG: the small video is dragged with the mouse or a finger and, let go,
    slides to the nearest of the four corners (the user's call). A top corner
    sits under the store's header, never on it.
  - ENLARGED: an autoplay («ambient») video had no controls at all there. It now
    gets the browser's own controls and its sound (the user's call: sound on
    with the enlarging, silent again once small), and three buttons of ours —
    from the start, back 10 s, forward 10 s. The buttons sit above the video,
    not on it: iPhones draw their own buttons in the video's top corners.
    A YouTube link is another site's player in a frame: enlarged it is loaded
    again with YouTube's controls and sound (it starts over), our three buttons
    cannot reach into it and are not shown, and it is dragged by its top strip.

| Variable | Type   | Description                                                  |
|----------|--------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| video    | string | direct file URL or YouTube link                              |
| poster   | string | optional poster image                                        |
| ambient  | bool   | true: muted autoplay loop, no controls while small · false: controls, the shopper presses play |

No Figma for it: sizes are our own. Style and script live here, not in app.css /
public js: only a page that uses the switch loads them, and the theme's CSS+JS
budget stays as it is. Nothing here passes the build, so directional values are
physical on purpose. One floating video per page: the first such block wins.
#}
<div data-qmini="{{ video }}"{% if poster %} data-qmini-poster="{{ poster }}"{% endif %}{% if ambient %} data-qmini-ambient{% endif %} hidden></div>
<style>
    .qmini {
        --qmini-gap: 24px;
        position: fixed;
        z-index: 890;                       /* under the offer pill (900), the header menus (1000) and the drawers */
        left: var(--qmini-gap);
        bottom: var(--qmini-gap);
        width: 360px;
        max-width: calc(100vw - 32px);
        aspect-ratio: var(--qmini-ar, 1.7778);
        overflow: hidden;
        border-radius: 16px;
        background: #000;
        box-shadow: 0 12px 36px rgba(23, 41, 81, .35);
        direction: ltr;
        animation: qmini-in .25s ease;
        /* dragged, not scrolled: a finger on the small video moves the video, not the page */
        touch-action: none;
        -webkit-user-select: none;
        user-select: none;
        cursor: grab;
    }
    .qmini--tall { width: 200px; }
    .qmini__player { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; object-fit: cover; }
    .qmini__bar {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        padding: 8px;
        pointer-events: none;
    }
    .qmini__bar button {
        pointer-events: auto;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        width: 32px;
        height: 32px;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        border: 0;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: rgba(13, 34, 54, .72);
        color: #fff;
        cursor: pointer;
    }
    .qmini__bar button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #91e6f7; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .qmini__bar svg { width: 16px; height: 16px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
    /* from the start · back 10 s · forward 10 s: with the enlarged video only */
    .qmini__more { display: none; gap: 10px; }

    /* the corner it was dropped nearest to (bottom-left until it is moved);
       a top corner starts under the store's header (--qmini-top, set by the script) */
    .qmini.qmini--r { left: auto; right: var(--qmini-gap); }
    .qmini.qmini--t { bottom: auto; top: calc(var(--qmini-top, 0px) + 12px); }
    .qmini.is-moved { animation: none; }
    .qmini.is-drag { cursor: grabbing; }
    .qmini.is-snap { transition: transform .25s cubic-bezier(.2, .8, .2, 1); }
    /* a YouTube frame keeps the pointer to itself: its top strip is the handle */
    .qmini--yt .qmini__bar { pointer-events: auto; }

    /* enlarged: centred over the page, as wide as the screen and its height allow;
       over the header (1000), still under the offer popups (9000) and the cart drawer (9999).
       Our buttons stand above the video (the box is lowered by half their strip to make the room). */
    .qmini-bd { display: none; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 8899; background: rgba(13, 34, 54, .6); }
    .qmini-bd.is-on { display: block; }
    .qmini.is-big {
        z-index: 8900;
        left: 50%;
        right: auto;
        top: calc(50% + 28px);
        bottom: auto;
        width: min(92vw, 960px, calc(84vh * var(--qmini-ar, 1.7778)));
        max-width: none;
        overflow: visible;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        transition: none;
        animation: none;
        touch-action: auto;
        cursor: auto;
    }
    .qmini.is-big .qmini__player { border-radius: 16px; }
    .qmini.is-big .qmini__bar { top: -56px; padding: 8px 0; pointer-events: none; }
    .qmini.is-big .qmini__bar button { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
    .qmini.is-big .qmini__bar svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
    .qmini.is-big .qmini__more { display: flex; }

    @keyframes qmini-in { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(16px); } }

    @media (min-width: 768px) {
        /* the store's WhatsApp button sits in the bottom-right corner: the video dropped there stands above it */
        body:has([id^="gb-widget"]) .qmini.qmini--r:not(.qmini--t):not(.is-big) { bottom: 96px; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
        /* phones: whatever already sits along the bottom edge lifts the video above itself —
           the offer pill (centre), the store's WhatsApp button (GetButton, 176 px wide on the
           right, it would cover the video's corner) and the «وصل للسلة» pill (full width) */
        body:has(.qj__pill:not([hidden])) { --qmini-pill: 68px; }
        body:has([id^="gb-widget"]) { --qmini-wa: 88px; }
        body:has(.qct.is-on) { --qmini-toast: 118px; }
        .qmini {
            --qmini-gap: 12px;
            bottom: max(16px, var(--qmini-pill, 0px), var(--qmini-wa, 0px), var(--qmini-toast, 0px));
            width: min(56vw, 240px);
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
        .qmini--tall { width: min(36vw, 150px); }
        .qmini.is-big { bottom: auto; width: min(92vw, calc(84vh * var(--qmini-ar, 1.7778))); }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .qmini { animation: none; } }
</style>
<script>
(function () {
  if (window.qissaMiniOn) { return; }            // one floating video per page: the first block wins
  window.qissaMiniOn = true;

  var src = document.querySelector('[data-qmini]');
  var url = src ? (src.getAttribute('data-qmini') || '').trim() : '';
  if (!url) { return; }
  var poster = src.getAttribute('data-qmini-poster');
  var ambient = src.hasAttribute('data-qmini-ambient');

  var WORDS = {{ {
      'close': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_close'),
      'expand': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_expand'),
      'shrink': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_shrink'),
      'restart': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_restart'),
      'back': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_back'),
      'forward': trans('blocks.qissa.mini_forward')
  }|json_encode|raw }};
  var ICON = {
    close: 'M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18',
    expand: 'M14 4h6v6M10 20H4v-6M20 4l-7 7M4 20l7-7',
    shrink: 'M21 3l-7 7M14 4v6h6M3 21l7-7M10 20v-6H4',
    restart: 'M19 19L9 12l10-7v14zM5 19V5',
    back: 'M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8M3 3v5h5',       // a turn to the left, «10» inside
    forward: 'M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-9-9c2.52 0 4.93 1 6.74 2.74L21 8M21 3v5h-5'    // a turn to the right, «10» inside
  };
  var TEN = '<text x="12" y="15.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8.5" font-weight="700" stroke="none" fill="currentColor">10</text>';

  // YouTube / Shorts -> id, matching the theme's other video blocks.
  function ytId(u) {
    var m = u.match(/(?:youtu\.be\/|youtube\.com\/(?:watch\?v=|embed\/|shorts\/|v\/))([\w-]{11})/);
    if (m) { return m[1]; }
    return /^[\w-]{11}$/.test(u) ? u : null;
  }
  function paint(b, name) {
    b.setAttribute('aria-label', WORDS[name]);
    b.innerHTML = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="' + ICON[name] + '"/>'
                + (name === 'back' || name === 'forward' ? TEN : '') + '</svg>';
  }
  function button(name, fn) {
    var b = document.createElement('button');
    b.type = 'button';
    paint(b, name);
    b.addEventListener('click', fn);
    return b;
  }

  function build() {
    var box = document.createElement('div');
    box.className = 'qmini';
    function ratio(ar) {
      box.style.setProperty('--qmini-ar', ar.toFixed(4));
      box.classList.toggle('qmini--tall', ar < 1);
    }

    var id = ytId(url), el;
    // the YouTube frame: ambient while small (silent loop, no controls); enlarged, YouTube's own controls and sound
    function yt(full) {
      return 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/' + id + '?rel=0&playsinline=1'
           + (ambient ? '&autoplay=1' + (full ? '' : '&mute=1&loop=1&controls=0&playlist=' + id) : '');
    }
    if (id) {
      el = document.createElement('iframe');
      el.src = yt(false);
      el.setAttribute('allow', 'autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen');
      el.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', '');
      el.setAttribute('title', 'video');
      box.classList.add('qmini--yt');
      if (url.indexOf('/shorts/') > -1) { ratio(9 / 16); }
    } else {
      el = document.createElement('video');
      el.playsInline = true;
      if (poster) { el.poster = poster; }
      if (ambient) {
        el.muted = true; el.autoplay = true; el.loop = true;
      } else {
        el.controls = true; el.preload = 'metadata';
      }
      el.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', function () {
        if (el.videoWidth && el.videoHeight) { ratio(el.videoWidth / el.videoHeight); }
      });
      el.src = url;
    }
    el.className = 'qmini__player';

    function play() { var p = el.play(); if (p && p.catch) { p.catch(function () {}); } }
    // to the start (by = 0) or by ± seconds, kept inside the video
    function seek(by) {
      if (!isFinite(el.duration)) { return; }
      el.currentTime = by ? Math.max(0, Math.min(el.duration, el.currentTime + by)) : 0;
      if (!by) { play(); }
    }

    var bd = document.createElement('div');
    bd.className = 'qmini-bd';
    var big = false;
    function size(on) {
      big = on;
      box.classList.remove('is-snap');
      box.style.transform = '';
      box.classList.toggle('is-big', on);
      bd.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
      paint(grow, on ? 'shrink' : 'expand');
      if (!ambient) { return; }                 // a video with controls keeps them, and its sound, at both sizes
      if (id) { el.src = yt(on); return; }
      // the ambient video: controls and sound while enlarged; small again it is the silent loop it was,
      // and plays on if it was paused — small, nothing could start it again
      el.controls = on;
      el.muted = !on;
      if (!on && el.paused) { play(); }
    }
    function esc(e) { if (e.key === 'Escape' && big) { size(false); } }

    // a top corner starts under the header: its full height, the inset it rides the hero with included
    var head = document.querySelector('.qheader');
    function inset() { box.style.setProperty('--qmini-top', (head ? head.offsetHeight : 0) + 'px'); }

    var grow = button('expand', function () { size(!big); });
    var close = button('close', function () {    // gone for this page view; removing the player stops it
      document.removeEventListener('keydown', esc);
      window.removeEventListener('resize', inset);
      document.removeEventListener('pointermove', move);
      document.removeEventListener('pointerup', drop);
      document.removeEventListener('pointercancel', drop);
      box.remove();
      bd.remove();
    });
    bd.addEventListener('click', function () { size(false); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', esc);
    window.addEventListener('resize', inset);
    inset();

    var bar = document.createElement('div');
    bar.className = 'qmini__bar';
    bar.appendChild(grow);
    if (!id) {
      var more = document.createElement('div');
      more.className = 'qmini__more';
      more.appendChild(button('restart', function () { seek(0); }));
      more.appendChild(button('back', function () { seek(-10); }));
      more.appendChild(button('forward', function () { seek(10); }));
      bar.appendChild(more);
    }
    bar.appendChild(close);
    box.appendChild(el);
    box.appendChild(bar);

    // ---- drag: the small video follows the pointer and, let go, slides to the nearest corner ----
    // The moves and the release are heard on the page, not on the video: a quick pointer is
    // outside the video before it has travelled far enough to count as a drag.
    var drag = null, dropped = 0;
    box.addEventListener('pointerdown', function (e) {
      if (big || !e.isPrimary || e.button > 0 || e.target.closest('button')) { return; }
      // a video showing the browser's controls: its bottom strip (play, the time bar) is theirs, not a handle
      if (!id && el.controls && e.clientY > box.getBoundingClientRect().bottom - 48) { return; }
      drag = { id: e.pointerId, x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY, on: false };
      // Where a press does nothing anyway (the silent loop, the YouTube strip) the pointer is held
      // from the start — over the YouTube frame its moves would go to YouTube. A video with
      // controls keeps its press (play / pause) and is held only once the drag is certain.
      if (id || !el.controls) { try { box.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch (err) { /* gone already */ } }
    });
    function move(e) {
      if (!drag || e.pointerId !== drag.id) { return; }
      if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' && !e.buttons) { drop(e); return; }     // let go where the page never heard it
      var dx = e.clientX - drag.x, dy = e.clientY - drag.y;
      if (!drag.on) {
        if (Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) < 8) { return; }     // a press, not a drag
        drag.on = true;
        box.classList.remove('is-snap');
        box.classList.add('is-drag', 'is-moved');
        try { box.setPointerCapture(drag.id); } catch (err) { /* gone already */ }
      }
      box.style.transform = 'translate(' + dx + 'px,' + dy + 'px)';
    }
    function drop(e) {
      if (!drag || e.pointerId !== drag.id) { return; }
      var moved = drag.on;
      drag = null;
      if (!moved) { return; }
      dropped = Date.now();
      box.classList.remove('is-drag');
      var from = box.getBoundingClientRect();
      box.classList.toggle('qmini--r', from.left + from.width / 2 > window.innerWidth / 2);
      box.classList.toggle('qmini--t', from.top + from.height / 2 < window.innerHeight / 2);
      box.style.transform = '';
      if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) { return; }
      // slide from where it was let go to its corner
      var to = box.getBoundingClientRect();
      box.style.transform = 'translate(' + (from.left - to.left) + 'px,' + (from.top - to.top) + 'px)';
      void box.offsetWidth;
      box.classList.add('is-snap');
      box.style.transform = '';
    }
    document.addEventListener('pointermove', move);
    document.addEventListener('pointerup', drop);
    document.addEventListener('pointercancel', drop);
    box.addEventListener('transitionend', function (e) { if (e.target === box) { box.classList.remove('is-snap'); } });
    // the click that ends a drag is not a press on the video
    box.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      if (Date.now() - dropped < 400) { e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); }
    }, true);

    // on <body>, not where the block stands: the home sections slide in with a transform
    // (.qreveal), and a transformed ancestor would pin a fixed child to itself
    document.body.appendChild(bd);
    document.body.appendChild(box);
  }

  // after the page has loaded, so the video never competes with the hero image (LCP)
  if (document.readyState === 'complete') { build(); } else { window.addEventListener('load', build); }
})();
</script>
